-- title:
--   Lift-valued Frobenius table from cubic base-change agreement
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with a group isomorphism $e \colon \operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$ satisfying `DetDictionaryRow`: for every prime $\ell \neq 3$ and every prime $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over $\ell$ with finite residue field and trivial inertia subgroup in $\operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$, the determinant of $e$ of the arithmetic Frobenius at $Q$ equals $\ell$ in $\mathbb{Z}/3$. For each of the three fixed fields $F$ attached to $\ker(\det \circ e)$, to `sylowH e` (the subgroup of elements whose image under $e$ is the reduction of a member of the explicit set `P16`) and to their intersection `quatH e`, there are given reals $c, u, d_1 < d_2$ with $c > 0$, $d_1 > 0$ and a finite set $T$ of points of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ such that the union of the right translates by the elements of $T$ of the centre-cut Siegel set with parameters $c, u, d_1, d_2$ covers $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ modulo left multiplication by $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ and right multiplication by central adelic scalars. Let $\Phi$ be a $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$-valued Hecke eigensystem over $\mathbb{Q}$ (a nonzero level ideal together with functions $a, b$ on the finite places) such that: the formal base change of $\Phi$ to the fixed field of `sylowH e` agrees, outside a finite set of places $w$ of that field, with the lift-trace seed $w \mapsto (\operatorname{tr}, \det)$ of the chosen $\{$`Slift`$,$`Tlift`$\}$-monoid lift of $e(\mathrm{Frob}_w^{\,f})$; and both $\Phi$ and its twist by `chiNegThreeWeight` satisfy `viaGeneralCuspNotion.IsCusp` over $\mathbb{Q}$, that is, each admits a continuous smooth cusp realisation of the complexified, centrally renormalised eigensystem which has the weight-one archimedean character and is holomorphic at every real place, and each has $b$ equal to $\chi_{-3}$ of the absolute norm away from a finite set of places. Then there is a finite set $T \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ of rational primes such that for every prime $\ell \notin T$ and every prime $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ over $\ell$ with finite residue field there exists a matrix $M$ in the submonoid of $M_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ generated by `Slift` and `Tlift` whose entrywise reduction under `red` ($\sqrt{-2} \mapsto -1$) is $e$ of the arithmetic Frobenius at $Q$, and with $\Phi.a$ at the place $\ell$ equal to $\operatorname{tr} M$ and $\Phi.b$ at $\ell$ equal to $\det M$.
--
--   This is the comparison step in the octahedral case of the Langlands–Tunnell theorem over $\mathbb{Q}$: it converts agreement of the cubic base change of $\Phi$ with the lift-trace table into the lift table over $\mathbb{Q}$ itself, resolving the cube-root ambiguity left by base change alone. It is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_isCusp_pair_of_detDictionaryRow_of_coversModCentre`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_isCusp_pair_of_detDictionaryRow_of_coversModCentre), where the Siegel-covering data and the cuspidal pair are supplied from the earlier construction.
